# Sample ~/.terminatorrc for Terminator
#
# Copy it with:   cp examples/terminatorrc ~/.terminatorrc
# or change bindings from inside Terminator with the `bind` builtin
# (`bind -l` lists the actions, `bind -R` restores every default).
#
# Format:  bind <action> <key>
# Keys:    modifiers Ctrl, Shift, Alt joined with '+', then a key name:
#          a letter/digit/symbol, Left, Right, Up, Down, Home, End, Tab,
#          PageUp, PageDown, Insert, Delete, Escape, Space, F1..F12.
#
# Invalid or conflicting lines are reported when Terminator starts (and when
# `bind` reloads the file); the affected action keeps its default key.
#
# Defaults:
#   cursor-left Left          cursor-right Right
#   line-start Ctrl+A         line-end Ctrl+E
#   history-prev Up           history-next Down
#   kill-line-start Ctrl+U    kill-line-end Ctrl+K
#   delete-word Ctrl+W        clear-screen Ctrl+L
#   eof Ctrl+D                interrupt Ctrl+C        suspend Ctrl+Z
#   copy Ctrl+Shift+C         paste Ctrl+Shift+V
#   history-search Ctrl+R    complete Tab
#   new-tab Ctrl+Shift+T      close-tab Ctrl+Shift+W
#   next-tab Ctrl+PageDown    prev-tab Ctrl+PageUp
#   scroll-up Shift+PageUp    scroll-down Shift+PageDown

# Examples (uncomment to use):
# bind history-search Alt+R
# bind new-tab Ctrl+Shift+N
# bind clear-screen F5
